## Tips and common pitfalls

- **The God component** (one box doing everything) and the **mystery arrow** (unlabelable data) are the two whiteboard smells — if you can't label the arrow, you've found a real design question. Good; answer it.
- **A straw-man alternative fools no one.** The alternative must be something a reasonable team might actually choose.
- **Trace the flow before you polish anything.** If your core user action doesn't traverse your components cleanly, the architecture isn't done, however pretty the diagram.
- **Un-owned state is the classic gap.** Every piece of data your flow touches must live in some box.
- **Write the doc you'd want to inherit.** In January, someone might.

